4:["$","main",null,{"className":"blog-page","children":[["$","$Le",null,{}],["$","article",null,{"className":"blog-article","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"shell blog-article-shell","children":[["$","$Lf",null,{"className":"blog-back-link","href":"/blog","children":[["$","$L10",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7","key":"1l729n"}],["path",{"d":"M19 12H5","key":"x3x0zl"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-left","size":16}]," All guides"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"blog-tag","children":["Admissions"," · ","One Window archive"]}],["$","h1",null,{"children":"List of Best Law Courses in Canada after 12th for Indian Students: Colleges, Eligibility & Ranking"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"blog-article-intro","children":"Students who want to study abroad in Canada can go through our list of best law courses in Canada after 12th for Indian students. One Window provides the information about overseas education in Canada, India student visa process and ranking of various colleges from across Canada which offer excellent courses like Bachelor of Laws (LLB), Bachelor of Commerce (BCom), Bachelors in Business Administration (BBA), etc. For more details, Read."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-article-body","children":[["$","section","Explore Top Colleges",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Explore Top Colleges"}],[["$","p","To study abroad on a student visa to Canada or to find higher education courses at overseas universities and colleges that accept international students who want to pursue law studies , consider doing a bit of research about various Canadian educational institutions offering law courses. To help you with your search, we’ve curated a list of some good colleges and universities offering law courses both at bachelors and post-graduate levels. For more details about these top law schools, read on.",{"children":"To study abroad on a student visa to Canada or to find higher education courses at overseas universities and colleges that accept international students who want to pursue law studies , consider doing a bit of research about various Canadian educational institutions offering law courses. To help you with your search, we’ve curated a list of some good colleges and universities offering law courses both at bachelors and post-graduate levels. For more details about these top law schools, read on."}],["$","p","Course Details",{"children":"Course Details"}],["$","p","A foreign student requires a study permit if they want to study at a university, college or other type of school in Canada. However, they are not required to hold a valid study permit while they’re studying at a designated learning institution (DLI). International students planning on doing any kind of coursework or training that takes more than six months will require an open work permit. You cannot apply for a work permit through your Study Permit; you have to apply separately by creating an account on Global Affairs Canada’s website.",{"children":"A foreign student requires a study permit if they want to study at a university, college or other type of school in Canada. However, they are not required to hold a valid study permit while they’re studying at a designated learning institution (DLI). International students planning on doing any kind of coursework or training that takes more than six months will require an open work permit. You cannot apply for a work permit through your Study Permit; you have to apply separately by creating an account on Global Affairs Canada’s website."}]],"$L11"]}],"$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c"]}],"$L1d"]}]}],"$L1e"]}]
